Manage owned tool window popups, which Autodesk Fusion uses for its palettes.

Wine maps "unmanaged" to X11 override-redirect, which tells the window manager
and the compositor not to touch the window at all: no stacking, no focus
handling, no WM_TRANSIENT_FOR. That is right for menus and tooltips, which live
for the duration of a click.

It is wrong for an owned WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW popup. That is a palette window. On
Windows it stays above its owner but drops behind another application when that
application is activated. Override-redirect makes that impossible, so Fusion's
docked sidebar floats above every other window on the desktop instead.

The rule is added as the last check in is_window_managed(), immediately before
the default "return FALSE". Every window reaching that point is unmanaged in
stock Wine, so the change can only flip unmanaged to managed and cannot alter
the outcome for any window Wine already manages. WS_EX_APPWINDOW in particular
keeps working.

The second hunk gives owned tool windows _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_UTILITY, which
EWMH defines as "a small persistent utility window, such as a palette or
toolbox". They previously got the dialog type, so window managers treated a
palette as a dialog of its owner.

This replaces wine-captionless-popups.patch, whose second hunk also made
captionless WS_EX_APPWINDOW popups and popups that own popups unmanaged. The
latter breaks make_owner_managed(): the owned window stays managed with
WM_TRANSIENT_FOR pointing at an override-redirect owner.

--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -463,6 +463,10 @@
     if (ex_style & WS_EX_APPWINDOW) return TRUE;
     /* windows that own popups are managed */
     if (has_owned_popups( hwnd )) return TRUE;
+    /* owned tool windows are palettes, they have to be stacked with their owner
+     * and to go behind other applications, which only the window manager can do */
+    if ((style & WS_POPUP) && (ex_style & WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW) &&
+        NtUserGetWindowRelative( hwnd, GW_OWNER )) return TRUE;
     /* default: not managed */
     return FALSE;
 }
@@ -1122,11 +1126,14 @@
         group_leader = owner_win;
     }
 
-    /* Only use dialog type for owned popups. Metacity allows making fullscreen
-     * only normal windows, and doesn't handle correctly TRANSIENT_FOR hint for
-     * dialogs owned by fullscreen windows.
+    /* Owned tool windows are palettes and toolboxes, which is what the utility
+     * type is for. Only use dialog type for the other owned popups. Metacity
+     * allows making fullscreen only normal windows, and doesn't handle correctly
+     * TRANSIENT_FOR hint for dialogs owned by fullscreen windows.
      */
-    if (((style & WS_POPUP) || (ex_style & WS_EX_DLGMODALFRAME)) && owner)
+    if ((ex_style & WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW) && owner)
+        window_set_net_wm_window_type( data, XATOM__NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_UTILITY );
+    else if (((style & WS_POPUP) || (ex_style & WS_EX_DLGMODALFRAME)) && owner)
         window_set_net_wm_window_type( data, XATOM__NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_DIALOG );
     else
         window_set_net_wm_window_type( data, XATOM__NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_NORMAL );
